      "targeted_symptom": "S011",
      "patient_response": "Hi, Dr. Smith. Nice to meet you too. Um, honestly, what made me come in is that I just keep getting up during our long sales strategy meetings. I know I’m supposed to stay seated, but I just... I end up getting up to refill my water or pace by the printer. \n\nWhich, actually, is so frustrating because our office printer is ancient. It constantly jams right when I need to print out a pitch for a client. I keep telling my boss we need a new one, but he's so weird about the budget lately. Like, he even downgraded the breakroom coffee to this awful store-brand powder. I can't even drink it, I have to walk down to the café on the corner now if I want anything decent. \n\nBut, um... wait, sorry, what was I saying? Oh, right, why I'm here. Yeah, I just can't seem to stay in my chair during those strategy meetings even though I know I'm supposed to just sit there.",
