    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you struggled with these kinds of focus or restlessness issues since you were a child, or is this a relatively new experience for you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, no, it's definitely not new. I remember this starting way, way before high school. Like, back in elementary school, my teachers were always writing on my report cards that I was bright but that I rushed through everything. And that I talked out of turn constantly. \n\nPlus I was always forgetting my homework because my desk was just... a complete disaster. It was always stuffed to the brim with half-finished papers. Actually, I remember my third-grade teacher, Mrs. Gable, making me dump my entire desk out on the floor once because the top wouldn't even close. All these crumpled worksheets fell out, along with this really old, squished juice box. It was grape juice, which is honestly the worst flavor anyway. Apple is clearly superior, but my mom always bought grape because it was on sale. She was always doing that, buying the weird off-brand snacks to save a few cents. I used to try to trade them at lunch, but nobody wants a generic grape juice box when the kid next to you has Gushers, you know? Like, it’s just not a fair trade in the cafeteria economy. \n\nBut, um... wait, what was the question? Oh, right, childhood. Yeah, so my teachers definitely noticed all that stuff really early on.",
