    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you also find that you frequently make careless mistakes in your work or struggle to pay close attention to details, even when you aren't feeling restless or impulsive?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, careless mistakes? I mean... I don't really think so. Not more than anyone else, anyway. Like, I definitely don't struggle with details when I'm actually sitting down and working. \n\nI mean, I'm in advertising sales, so you have to be pretty sharp with the numbers, right? Though, honestly, some of the clients we deal with don't even look at the numbers. They just want a flashy ad. We had this one guy last week who wanted us to put his face on a billboard, but he wanted his dog in it too. A pug. Which, pugs are cute, but they always look like they're struggling to breathe. I saw a documentary once about how they were bred to look like that, and it's actually really sad. It makes you think about how weird humans are, just breeding animals to look a certain way. Like those hairless cats. Why would anyone want a cat that looks like a raw chicken? My aunt had one, and it always felt so warm and weird when it sat on your lap. She used to knit it little sweaters in the winter so it wouldn't freeze. \n\nWait, sorry. Did you ask about my work? Yeah, I don't really think I make a lot of careless mistakes. I'm pretty good about catching things when I'm focused.",
